<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabella Jagiellon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1559">1559</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Izabela Jagiellonka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabella Jagiellon was a Polish princess, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-i-the-old">Sigismund I the Old</a>, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, in 1539. After his death in 1540 she governed the eastern Hungarian kingdom as regent for their infant son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-zapolya">John Sigismund</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-martinuzzi">George Martinuzzi</a>. She ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1551 but returned in 1556, helping lay the foundations of the Principality of Transylvania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabella-jagiellon.jpg" alt="Isabella Jagiellon" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cranach_the_Younger_Isabella_Jagiellon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
